  "description": "Veto exception: when vetoes would leave zero finalists they are ignored for ranking (but still reported), so the round never reaches a state with no options",
  "spec_clause": "Phase 2 / Veto: 'Exception: if vetoes leave fewer than two finalists, ignore them for ranking but surface them prominently in the UI. Never reach a state with no options.'",
  "rationale": "3 attendees, two finalists. m1: rows u1,u2 yes / u3 no -> attendee_votes 3, coverage 1.00, yes 2, approval 2/3 = 0.6667. m2: rows u1,u3 yes / u2 no -> yes 2, approval 0.6667. Both clear the floor and both fit in N_FINALISTS = 5; they tie on yes-votes but the tie is not at the boundary so only the finalist SET is asserted. Vetoes: u3 vetoes m1 (count 1 >= 1) and u2 vetoes m2 (count 1 >= 1) -> applying them would disqualify both and leave 0 finalists, which is fewer than two -> the exception fires: vetoes are ignored for ranking and both movies stay in the round robin. m1 vs m2: m2 preferred by u1,u3 = 2, m1 by u2 = 1 -> m2 beats m1 = Condorcet winner. Side effects still apply: u3's standing vote on m1 was already no and stays no; u2's standing yes on m2 flips to no.",
